From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: blurbery <271863866+blurbery@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] vd_lavc: tolerate a short burst of hardware decoding errors

vd_lavc gives up on a hardware decoder for the rest of the file as soon
as a run of consecutive decoding errors reaches --hwdec-software-fallback.
With that option set to yes (1), a single frame the hardware decoder
rejects after playback has started switches the whole title to software
decoding.

Keep that behaviour while probing, before the decoder has output a frame
(hwdec_notified unset). Once it has, a run that reaches the option's
count ends hardware decoding only after two keyframe packets have been
sent during the run without recovering, or once the run reaches 240
errors. A keyframe accepted by avcodec_send_packet() during a run (any
result other than EAGAIN or EOF) counts before that packet's own error.
Both counts are reset only by a decoded frame, which logs a warning that
hardware decoding recovered, and when the decoder is torn down; seeks and
other flushes keep them. A copy-back failure still falls back at once.

Applies to mpv v0.41.0 on top of Vivid's patches 0001 and 0002.

Licence: this patch is part of Vivid's Lucid Engine patch series for mpv.
Like the file it modifies, it is free software; you can redistribute it
and/or modify it under the terms of the GNU Lesser General Public License
